SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari’s Speech at the Signing of Electoral Bill 2022","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-speech-at-the-signing-of-electoral-bill-2022/","claim":"Buhari said the 2022 Electoral Act would improve transparency, effectiveness, and the use of technology in Nigerian elections.","locator":"paragraphs 2-4, lines 28-31","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential speech on a law he assented to; authoritative for intent and formal action, though self-serving.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 pre-election reform period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari action, though implementation depended on INEC and the National Assembly.","contrary_evidence":["Self-justifying rhetoric","later observers reported implementation gaps and disputes around the new rules"],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari’s Speech at the Signing of Electoral Bill 2022","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-speech-at-the-signing-of-electoral-bill-2022/","claim":"Buhari said section 84(12) conflicted with the constitution and asked the National Assembly to amend the bill by deleting that section.","locator":"paragraphs 6-12, lines 33-41","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential speech with explicit language about the requested amendment and legal rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 electoral-law fight.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari action; this shows an executive attempt to change the rules around political appointee participation.","contrary_evidence":["He still assented to the broader reform package","the legislature later refused to follow his amendment request"],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.5","4B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement of the First Joint NDI/IRI Pre-Election Assessment Mission to Nigeria","publisher":"International Republican Institute","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://www.iri.org/news/statement-of-the-first-joint-ndi-iri-pre-election-assessment-mission-to-nigeria/","claim":"The mission said the 2022 Electoral Act enjoyed wide stakeholder support and improved INEC's ability to deliver more transparent elections through clearer timelines, technology, and earlier funding.","locator":"lines 45-61, 99-100","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent election-observation mission after meetings with INEC, National Assembly, parties, civil society, media, security forces, and diplomats.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 pre-election environment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material because Buhari assented to the law and its early effects were under his administration.","contrary_evidence":["The mission warned full implementation was uncertain","INEC was not yet fully funded by the government as mandated by law"],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement of the First Joint NDI/IRI Pre-Election Assessment Mission to Nigeria","publisher":"International Republican Institute","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://www.iri.org/news/statement-of-the-first-joint-ndi-iri-pre-election-assessment-mission-to-nigeria/","claim":"The mission said women, youth, persons with disabilities, and internally displaced persons still faced major barriers to political participation, even though some parties had reduced nomination fees and added marginalized delegates.","locator":"lines 72-74, 96-100, 135-140","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent mission report with specific findings on candidate access and inclusion gaps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect; this describes the political environment Buhari governed rather than a single presidential order.","contrary_evidence":["Some parties reduced fees for women aspirants","APC and PDP added women/PWD delegates"],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.7","4B.10"]}
